  {
    "id": "anno-kano_upper_p097_left-15",
    "type": "Annotation",
    "body": [
      {
        "purpose": "transcribing",
        "value": "寺　百七十三戸"
      },
      {
        "purpose": "modern_jp_reading",
        "value": "寺　百七十三戸"
      },
      {
        "purpose": "english_translation",
        "value": "Temples: 173 households. This is a second temple entry, distinct from the 101 temples counted three columns to the right, and it gives a household figure rather than a building or head count. I cropped its label glyph and the earlier 寺 side by side at eight times magnification: both show 土 over 寸 with no 礻 radical, so this is 寺 and not 社. The project's dataset carries no row for this column; the note on its 姓 row records only that the figure 173 was once filed under 姓 and then removed. Counting these 173 households in the household schedule brings the components to 6,308 against the printed total of 6,305, while leaving them out falls 170 short — so they do belong to the schedule."
      },
      {
        "purpose": "identifying",
        "value": "寺戸數"
      }
    ],
    "target": {
      "source": "images/upper_p097_left.jpg",
