        "value": "Sei: 258 persons. The source prints the bare label 姓 with no gloss and no household figure. It stands between the temple entries and the eta and hinin returns, so it denotes a small registered status group separate both from the 5,387 peasant households recorded on the facing leaf and from the 681 townsman households recorded here."
